#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Leave a text for the person on this session's card. Run by the session itself.

    paste create <session-id> [--provider claude] --title "Message to Sven" [--secret] <file>     prints the new id
    paste withdraw <session-id> [--provider claude] <paste-id>
    paste sweep

Name the provider when you know it: two providers may use the same session id,
and a Paste with a provider belongs to that provider's session alone.

The text comes from a file, never from an argument: quotes, backslashes and
line breaks do not survive a shell. Withdraw a Paste only when you have seen
that it was used (the mail is sent, the policy is live).

A password, token or key goes into the person's login keyring, never into a
file: say `--secret`, and a token or password found in the text counts without
it. The command refuses, and writes nothing, when the keyring cannot be reached
(it is unlocked by logging in). Keep a title free of secrets, since the card
shows it in the clear, and delete the file you wrote the text in once you have
made the Paste. `sweep` is for after a crash: it removes keyring items no Paste
points at and names Pastes whose item is gone.
"""
import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))
import paste

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(paste.main())
